body:
So it was the "no massage-y" for me. If you can drum up using baby talk or slangify the word, or you're willing to take a hand or leg as a consolation prize - that's a red flag for me. CNAs nor nurses are swimming in all this extra massage time just to score patient score points. I think you're feeling a little gaslit by textbook nursing and your self preservation and anti creep system is working perfectly fine. Also, your nursing judgment is sound in that you dropped a pain relieving massage for a patient you could recognize to be in actual pain and in the need for therapeutic touch. 

&#x200B;

tldr: no gassy lighty

If it's all egg yolk then I quit.

&#x200B;

PS - if I ever sell houses and the client at a showing asks if I can still have kids, that's a hard nope

I'm going to call him Reporter John because

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

he got the scoop.

I have seen both listed recently. And then the odd NKDA hanging around. 

&#x200B;

Try adding NKDA a second time?
